<title>UK: LIFFE white sugar ends steadier, range narrow.</title>
<headline>LIFFE white sugar ends steadier, range narrow.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>White sugar futures edged slightly higher during Monday evening LIFFE trading, continuing the pattern of narrow-range movements, traders said.</p>
<p>Spread business largely dominated trading throughout, with little emerging from the physical sector.</p>
<p>August finished at $310.80 a tonne, up $1.60 from Friday, while October was $0.60 higher at $305.30. LIFFE turnover was 1,267 lots.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
